# Testing & Quality Assurance

## No test runner is configured yet

**This entire file is aspirational guidance for if/when a test runner is
added.** `package.json` has no Vitest/Jest, no `@testing-library/react`, no
`test` script — nothing here currently runs. Don't imply to a teammate (or
in a PR) that these tests exist or pass today; treat this as the intended
shape for test code once a runner (Vitest is the natural fit for a Vite
project) is deliberately added, not as documentation of current behavior.

## Target Testing Stack (once adopted)
- **Unit Testing**: React Testing Library + Vitest (or Jest)
- **E2E Testing**: Playwright or Cypress (recommended)
- **Accessibility Testing**: axe-core + `jest-axe`/`vitest-axe`
- **Visual Testing**: Storybook (optional)

## React Testing Library Patterns

### Component Testing
```javascript
// src/components/messages/__tests__/MessageBubble.test.jsx
import React from 'react'
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react'
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event'
import MessageBubble from '../MessageBubble'

const mockMessage = {
  id: '1',
  text: 'Hey, check out this track!',
  senderId: 'user-1',
  formattedTime: '10:32 AM'
}

describe('MessageBubble', () => {
  it('renders message content correctly', () => {
    render(<MessageBubble message={mockMessage} onReact={() => {}} />)

    expect(screen.getByText('Hey, check out this track!')).toBeInTheDocument()
    expect(screen.getByText('10:32 AM')).toBeInTheDocument()
  })

  it('calls onReact when clicked', async () => {
    const user = userEvent.setup()
    const mockOnReact = vi.fn()

    render(<MessageBubble message={mockMessage} onReact={mockOnReact} />)

    await user.click(screen.getByRole('button'))
    expect(mockOnReact).toHaveBeenCalledWith('1')
  })

  it('applies own-message styling when isOwnMessage is true', () => {
    render(<MessageBubble message={mockMessage} onReact={() => {}} isOwnMessage />)

    const bubble = screen.getByRole('button')
    expect(bubble).toHaveStyle('align-self: flex-end')
  })
})
```

### Form Testing
```javascript
// src/components/auth/__tests__/LoginForm.test.jsx
import React from 'react'
import { render, screen, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react'
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event'
import LoginForm from '../LoginForm'

describe('LoginForm', () => {
  it('validates required fields', async () => {
    const user = userEvent.setup()
    const mockSubmit = vi.fn()

    render(<LoginForm onSubmit={mockSubmit} />)

    const submitButton = screen.getByRole('button', { name: /log in/i })
    await user.click(submitButton)

    expect(screen.getByText('Email is required')).toBeInTheDocument()
    expect(screen.getByText('Password is required')).toBeInTheDocument()
    expect(mockSubmit).not.toHaveBeenCalled()
  })

  it('submits form with valid credentials', async () => {
    const user = userEvent.setup()
    const mockSubmit = vi.fn()

    render(<LoginForm onSubmit={mockSubmit} />)

    await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(/email/i), 'user@rhynk.app')
    await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(/password/i), 'hunter2hunter2')

    await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /log in/i }))

    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(mockSubmit).toHaveBeenCalledWith({
        email: 'user@rhynk.app',
        password: 'hunter2hunter2'
      })
    })
  })

  it('shows loading state during submission', async () => {
    const user = userEvent.setup()
    const mockSubmit = vi.fn(() => new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100)))

    render(<LoginForm onSubmit={mockSubmit} />)

    await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(/email/i), 'user@rhynk.app')
    await user.type(screen.getByLabelText(/password/i), 'hunter2hunter2')

    const submitButton = screen.getByRole('button', { name: /log in/i })
    await user.click(submitButton)

    expect(screen.getByText('Logging in...')).toBeInTheDocument()
    expect(submitButton).toBeDisabled()
  })
})
```

